                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I have put 500 hours into the game. Back when Hudell was in charge, I would have recommended it to the moon and back. I made a new save and replayed it every time there was an update. Once he stepped down, everything changed. The graphics were improved, but that was about it. \n\nThe controls feel terrible to play with. They redid the game on a new engine from the ground up, so the previous fluid controls were replaced with a clunky mess (at least on PC), that makes playing extremely frustrating. They redid the entire town and layout, but did not include a new map. After over six months of having no map, they gave us a 'map' that didn't actually show you where anything was. Do you want to find the blacksmith? Good luck, the map doesn't show where anything is located. If you're lost, you're going to be lost and waste your time. \n\nMarriage, and other core functions of the game are missing. Forageables are everywhere, sell for a good amount, and respawn, so it's an infinite money glitch, making farming and doing much of anything else pointless.  The new devs seem passionless about this game, and just wanted to push something out and call it good enough so that they can be done with it and make some money. They don't communicate on their discord or give us any transparency on what's going on, what they're planning for the future (if anything), or why they're making the decisions they've made. Unless they step up, I cannot recommend this game. There are so many, better farming games out there to play instead, whose devs deserve your support.\n\nEdit on Dec 6th:  Over a month has passed, and I've seen no communication on either steam or their discord about the missing features in the 1.0 release. There have been a few bug fix patches, but that is all. When are we going to see real improvements? What improvements are going to be made? What missing features that were PROMISED to us when we bought the game, are actually going to be implemented down the line, and when? Communication and action would have been a nice way to try to build back trust with players who used to love the game, but I guess yall couldn't be bothered? I feel so scammed. I would have never bought the game without the guarantee of certain features that were not in the 1.0 release. I wish I qualified for a refund.\n\nEdit on Oct 11th, 2025: Almost a year has passed, and there has, so far, been no effort to add the content that was promised to us. There has been no major improvements, nothing of value added. Only a few bug fixes. Now, they are handing off the future development of this game to another team, with no transparency on who that team is or what content they will be working on. Will we get romance that was promised to us in Early Access? Will we get a functional map that's actually useful? Will we get better tool upgrades and more story? Will we get back the fantasy elements and cultural aspects that drew us in the first place??? Probably not. While this other team is doing mysterious work on Orange Season, the original team has decided to create a new game. Because that worked so well the last time. They've broken trust with me every step of the way, and think they can wipe their hands clean and start over fresh. I wouldn't recommend ANY project that this studio, or team, has or will work on in the future. They've destroyed what I once loved so much, and I have no hope that it will ever be made whole again.\n\nEdit on Oct 11th, 2026. Another year has passed us by. And what has changed? Besides a few patches, absolutely nothing. The mysterious new team that was supposed to work on a content update has never been mentioned since, and no update has appeared. There has still been no communication about what, if anything, is going on. And their new game has been released, which also seems riddled with bugs and not fit for launch, but I haven't played it myself. I've written this update, and the original review, in hurt, anger, and resentment, but I'm happy that it seems to be helpful to others. Thank you for reading this. If you're reading this after buying the game to see if other people have had the same negative experience you have had but you can not longer refund it, I'm sorry. If you truly enjoy the game for what it is, I'm happy for you. But I'll always be angry and sad that it never became what it could have been.",
